@startuml
title NitroCircus - Operational Flow

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

actor PO as "Product Owner"
participant BOT as "Telegram Bot"
participant API as "Orchestrator API"
participant PM as "PM Agent"
database DB as "MongoDB"
queue REDIS as "Redis"
participant GH as "GitHub"
participant RUNNER as "agent-runner"
participant LLM as "Execution Provider"

== Create ==
PO -> BOT : /new <descripcion>
BOT -> API : project.create
API -> DB : create Project(state=draft)
API --> BOT : project created
BOT --> PO : confirmación

== Plan ==
PO -> BOT : /plan <project>
BOT -> API : project.plan
API -> PM : analizar y descomponer
PM --> API : épicas + tareas + agentes + criterios
API -> DB : persist Project/Epic/Task
API -> GH : create Issues + labels + board items
API -> DB : tasks -> awaiting_start_approval
BOT --> PO : resumen y tareas listas

== Start ==
PO -> BOT : /start <project>
BOT -> API : project.start
API -> DB : tasks -> in_progress
API -> REDIS : enqueue by agent queue
API -> GH : issues -> status:in_progress
BOT --> PO : inicio autorizado

== Execution ==
REDIS -> RUNNER : BRPOP task
RUNNER -> LLM : ejecutar tarea
RUNNER -> GH : commit + push branch
RUNNER -> API : task.agent_complete(in_review|blocked)
API -> DB : transition task
API -> GH : labels / board sync
API --> BOT : estado disponible para /status

== Approval ==
PO -> BOT : /approve <task-id>
BOT -> API : task.approve
API -> DB : task -> done
API -> GH : close issue + board -> Done
BOT --> PO : aprobado

note over API,DB
La transición de estados siempre pasa por la API.
El runner no cambia estado directamente en DB ni en GitHub.
end note

@enduml

